# Union-merge append-only data files as a last-resort guard for manual or legacy
# concurrent data commits. The production Phase 2 path is now artifact-first and
# single-writer, but these files are still safest as append-only merges.
#
# Without this, Git's default recursive merge with `-X ours` can silently drop
# overlapping manual recovery rows: Git's patch-similarity heuristic may see
# two append hunks at the same file offset and mark the later patch as already
# upstream. Union merge concatenates both sides' hunks, which is exactly what
# we want for append-only CSVs.
#
# Do NOT add JSON files here — union merge produces invalid JSON by
# concatenating conflicting objects. Single-writer discipline (Phase 1 only,
# self-hosted runner serializes) is how JSON files stay consistent.
box-office-tracker/data/seat-counts.csv         merge=union
box-office-tracker/data/pre-reservation-snapshots.csv merge=union
box-office-tracker/data/polymarket-markets.csv  merge=union
